{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPaY9mwzTAjGcciW86VM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `needs-network` worker status is implemented and the tests I ran pass. I did not run `make lint test`, the whole repository's tests, or `make docs-check` (mkdocs isn't installed here).\n\nA worker role file with `status: needs-network` and a valid `network:` list now closes out as `OutcomeNeedsNetwork`. It ends `ard:needs-human`, with one comment listing each entry and its URL in a code span. The Reaper close-out, which has no worker result, gets the same plan.\n\n- **Parsing:** the list takes 1–10 entries, each with `what`, `url`, `why` and an optional `verify`. `url` must be https, at most 300 bytes, with no userinfo. Text fields are one line, at most 200 runes. The list is rejected with any other status, and `needs-network` is rejected on a non-worker stage.\n- **Redaction:** the plan takes the list from the redacted re-parse. If it no longer parses, the job ends `needs-human` with \"network list unreadable after redaction\".\n- **Other code:** the cost table and the Reaper's two outcome switches handle the new outcome like `needs-human`. `docs/proposal.md` has the contract and worker loop step 9.\n\nI added tests for the parser table cases, `Build` (including the Reaper), `Prepare` and the comment. `go test` on `internal/closeout`, `internal/costs` and `internal/reaper` passes, and `go vet` on those packages is clean.\n\nI did not add a Run-level test in `closer_test.go`. That \"nothing pushed, no PR\" behaviour rests on `internal/worker/run.go` already treating any non-done status that way. I read that code but didn't exercise it in a test.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/384/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":963,"cache_read_input_tokens":48382,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_inpu